Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=(), event=Decided(decision='ciworkflows', at=datetime(2026, 10, 13, 0, 0, 0), actor='owner', title='CI has two workflows sized for two events; the APK builds only when the Android shell changed or MAJOR moves', body="*A release is a `v<version>` tag*, made by `train.sh land` alone, and CI has two workflows sized for two events (after September's included Actions minutes ran out on the 12th; one run had been eighty minutes of six sandboxes each compiling the workspace from zero). `quick.yml` runs on every push to master: the commit check and `check` (fmt, clippy, docs) from `cargo` against a restored dependency build with one set of flags (`.github/cargo-ci.toml`), not run again on git tree entries that already passed, so a docs change costs the commit check alone; the suite and the browser are the merge gate's. `tests.yml` runs on a `v*.*.0` tag (a train that moved MINOR or MAJOR; every train tags, and a patch is not worth an hour of runner) and a manual dispatch: the Nix derivations — release, fixture, both checks, both generators — from crane's one shared dependency build, which no release moves. `release-apk.yml` builds the APK only when the Android shell (`android/`, `nix/apk.nix`, the icon) changed since the previous tag, or the tag starts a new MAJOR (the owner, 2026-10-13): the web app updates itself behind the portal. 1.10.0 (2026-10-12) was cut by hand, the last one, to close the 0.17.0 drift; `v1.0.0` names a release commit that never reached master.", rationale="Incident: September's included Actions minutes ran out on the 12th; one run had been eighty minutes of six sandboxes each compiling the workspace from zero. The owner, 2026-10-13, on the APK. 1.10.0 (2026-10-12) was the last release cut by hand.", supersedes=()))